        "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-text\">client server at Beget\n  -&gt; nightly backup of database and files (pull, 01:00)\n  -&gt; backup server outside Beget, restic\n  -&gt; weekly restore check\n  -&gt; new server in Yandex Cloud (Terraform, Ansible)\n  -&gt; restored portal\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Problem</h2>\n<p>The client kept a self-hosted Bitrix24 server at the hosting provider Beget. The full portal worked on this server: CRM, chats with customers, tasks and business processes.</p>\n<p>On 2 November 2026 Beget had a large outage. On 3 November the nightly backup could not connect to the client server. For more than a week Beget says nothing about the data on this server. Most likely, the data is lost.</p>\n<h2>What I did</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>In September 2026 I built a backup system. Every night it pulls the portal database and files to a separate server outside Beget. The client server cannot delete its own backups.</li>\n<li>Once a week the system checks the backup by itself: it loads the database into a temporary MySQL and counts the tables. On 8 November the check confirmed: the backup of 2 November can be restored, the database has 1768 tables.</li>\n<li>On 9 November I wrote the new server as Terraform code and created it in Yandex Cloud in 41 seconds. I raised the cloud quotas in advance.</li>\n<li>I wrote the Bitrix server setup as Ansible code. I found and went around a bug of the official installer on the cloud image.</li>\n<li>During the copy, the network card of the office backup server failed. From a console photo I found the cause and made the fix permanent.</li>\n<li>I ran the restore as a separate service. A VPN or SSH drop does not stop it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The backup saved the data: Beget cannot return it for more than a week, but the client has its own copy of 2 November.</li>\n<li>5.4 GB of files and the portal database are on the new server. The restore took 34 minutes.</li>\n<li>The domain moved to the new server on the same day.</li>\n<li>The new server, its setup and the restore are code. A repeat move is a few commands.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How it looks</h2>\n<p>These are real screenshots from the work. The client name, addresses and IDs are covered in red.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"/assets/cases/img/portal-restore/backups-verify.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"649\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Backup server output: last snapshots, the connection failure on 3 November and the successful check on 8 November\">\n  <figcaption>Backup server: last snapshots of 2 November, the failed connection to the client server on 3 November and the weekly check on 8 November - OK, 1768 tables. The log is in Russian.</figcaption>\n</figure><figure>\n  <img src=\"/assets/cases/img/portal-restore/yandex-cloud-vm.webp\" width=\"1430\" height=\"355\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Yandex Cloud console: the new server with the label managed-by terraform\">\n  <figcaption>Yandex Cloud: the new server is created by Terraform, see the label managed-by: terraform.</figcaption>\n</figure><figure>\n  <img src=\"/assets/cases/img/portal-restore/nic-hang-photo.webp\" width=\"760\" height=\"367\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Console photo of the office server: Detected Hardware Unit Hang errors\">\n  <figcaption>Console photo of the office backup server: the network card hangs under load (Detected Hardware Unit Hang).</figcaption>\n</figure><figure>\n  <img src=\"/assets/cases/img/portal-restore/nic-fix.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"569\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Terminal: hardware packet offload is off, the speed is 1000 Mb/s\">\n  <figcaption>The fix is permanent: hardware packet offload is off, the speed is 1000 Mb/s again, no new failures.</figcaption>\n</figure><h2>More</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/assets/cases/en/05-portal-restore.pdf\">Case with real screenshots, PDF</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>I do not publish the client name, server addresses or private data.</p>"
